Scenario 1: Static CALL
1. Write MAINPGM source.
2. Write SUBPGM source.
3. Compile both programs.
4. Link-edit the Main Program with the Subprogram object module.
5. Execute the linked load module.
Scenario 2: Dynamic CALL
1. Compile MAINPGM.
2. Compile SUBPGM separately.
3. Place the Subprogram load module in an accessible load library.
4. Execute MAINPGM.
5. When MAINPGM executes CALL, the system loads/resolves SUBPGM.
The exact compile and binder JCL depends on your site's compiler procedures and load-library setup.
